      <rules>
        <rule id="6881f089-9fc4-5d19-af7f-760ffe49d7bb" name="Create Panic" hidden="false">
          <description>This model displaces all models when it moves, place them up to 1” Away. Immobile units prevent this model from moving there.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="9d064a3d-e6de-5bdd-ac5e-2754aa45f9df" name="Immense Bulk" hidden="false">
          <description>This model may only Pivot up to its current M value. It may still move as normal.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="e769128f-dee8-5172-bd27-0b76ca42c6a1" name="Landing Pad" hidden="false">
          <description>This model may</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="509e51b9-a01f-55fd-8e54-46cafac6ea13" name="transport 1" hidden="false">
          <description>non-Titanic High Altitude or Flyer Vehicle. Embarked models may Repair d3 Wounds and have secondary services restored on a 3+.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="14a46b33-bd67-57c7-b681-fb70358d66ba" name="The Hour is Nigh" hidden="false">
          <description>When the weapon is fired, place a marker on field at a valid target. In your next Command Phase, the missile strikes! Scatter like normal, following the 15” Blast radius rules.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="3bcbd3bd-be45-5d5e-8fc2-863d727fb901" name="T Minus 5" hidden="false">
          <description>The weapon may not be fired Turn 1. The weapon cannot be destroyed or Disabled. If the weapon is marked on the field and the carrier is destroyed, the Deathstrike Missile still hits in your Command Phase.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
